// [LOCAL] Ships the dictionary inside the dll as the factory default.
//
// Why both a built-in copy AND the external file:
//   - The external file (<game>\T7Patch\translate_zh.txt) still WINS whenever it
//     exists.  That is what keeps "edit the text file, see it in game two
//     seconds later, no rebuild" working - the whole point of keeping it out of
//     the dll in the first place.
//   - The built-in copy is what makes the install self-contained (nothing to
//     copy next to d3d11.dll) and what keeps translation alive when the external
//     file is missing, corrupt or empty - before this, losing that one file
//     silently disabled the whole feature.
//
// [LOCAL] The resource points at a PINNED SNAPSHOT, not at the live dictionary.
//   - It deliberately reads translate_zh.builtin.txt, NOT the file the project
//     keeps editing (translate/translate_zh.txt).  Pointing it straight at the
//     live file meant every code rebuild silently shipped whatever state the
//     dictionary happened to be in at that moment - including half-finished
//     edits - so the built-in could never be reasoned about.
//   - Refreshing the snapshot is a DELIBERATE release step, and the only moment
//     the built-in ever moves forward:
//       1. finish the dictionary and push it (players receive it through the
//          overlay's update button, or a deploy - the built-in never follows by
//          itself, and it never has to);
//       2. copy translate/translate_zh.txt over translate/translate_zh.builtin.txt
//          (a byte copy, sha256 must match);
//       3. recompile.
//   - Verify with .workbuddy\ref\embed_verify.py: it compares the image against
//     the PINNED file and must say "BYTE-IDENTICAL to source : True".  It also
//     prints how far the live dictionary has drifted ahead of the snapshot.
//
// Consequence: this resource only needs recompiling when the snapshot is
// refreshed - i.e. on a release.  Editing translate_zh.txt for the running game
// never needs a rebuild.
//
// The path is relative to this .rc file (rc.exe resolves relative paths against
// the directory of the resource script), i.e.
// <repo>\translate\translate_zh.builtin.txt.

#include <windows.h>
#include "translate_res.h"

IDR_TRANSLATE_DICT RCDATA "..\\translate\\translate_zh.builtin.txt"
